<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} head={head}>
<main id="main"><div class="container"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="index.html">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page"><span>Investment Property Loans in Miami</span></li></ol></nav></div><section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Rental property financing</p><h1>Investment Property Loans in Miami</h1><p>Compare financing options for Miami rental properties, investor condos, DSCR loans, and cash-out refinance scenarios.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Compare Investor Loans</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Calculate Rental Payment</a></div><div class="trust-row"><span class="trust-pill">Matthew Gromadzki</span><span class="trust-pill">NMLS #2560919</span><span class="trust-pill">Miami · Florida</span><span class="trust-pill">Call (305) 988-4806</span></div></div><div class="hero-panel rate-card"><div class="rate-item"><span>Best first step</span><strong>Preapproval</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Core review</span><strong>Payment + cash to close</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Miami focus</span><strong>Condo + jumbo checks</strong></div><a class="btn btn-primary full" href="start.html">Send Scenario</a></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container two-col"><article class="prose"><p>Investment property financing in Miami requires a clear look at cash flow, down payment, property type, insurance, taxes, association dues, rental restrictions, and long-term strategy.</p><p>Depending on the scenario, investors may compare conventional investor loans, DSCR loans, bank statement options, portfolio loans, and cash-out refinance structures.</p><h2>Investor loan factors</h2><p>Lenders may review credit, reserves, rental income, property condition, occupancy, entity ownership, condo eligibility, insurance, and market rent. The documentation approach depends on the loan type.</p><p>For Miami condos, association rules and short-term rental restrictions can make or break the investment plan.</p><h2>Plan the full payment</h2><p>Investors should calculate principal and interest, taxes, insurance, HOA dues, assessments, vacancy, repairs, management, and reserves. A lower rate alone does not guarantee a better investment.</p><p>The best loan structure should match the property’s cash flow and your exit strategy.</p></article><aside><form class="lead-form lead-form-compact" method="post" action="quote.html" data-lead-form><h2>Request a Investment Property Loans Miami Quote</h2><p>Answer a few basics and we’ll review the best mortgage path for your scenario.</p><input type="hidden" name="source_page" value="preview"><label>Loan goal<select name="loan_goal" required><option value="">Select one</option><option>Buying a home</option><option>Refinancing</option><option>Cash-out refinance</option><option>Investment property</option><option>Condo financing</option></select></label><div class="form-row"><label>Purchase price / value<input name="property_value" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$650,000"></label><label>Down payment / equity<input name="down_payment" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$100,000"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Credit score range<select name="credit_score"><option value="">Select range</option><option>760+</option><option>720–759</option><option>680–719</option><option>640–679</option><option>Below 640</option><option>Not sure</option></select></label><label>Property city<input name="property_city" placeholder="Miami"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Name<input name="name" autocomplete="name" required></label><label>Phone<input name="phone" autocomplete="tel" required></label></div><label>Email<input name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required></label><button class="btn btn-primary full" type="submit">Start Mortgage Review</button><p class="form-note">No obligation. Mortgage options depend on underwriting, lender guidelines, property type, and documentation.</p></form></aside></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="container"><div class="cta-band"><div><p class="eyebrow">Fast next step</p><h2>Get a mortgage scenario review before you make a decision.</h2><p>Send purchase price, down payment, credit range, income type, and property city. The goal is to compare real options, not guess based on generic rates.</p></div><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Start Review</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="tel:+13059884806">Call (305) 988-4806</a></div></div></div></section><section class="section faq-section"><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>Investment Property Loans in Miami FAQ</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Can I use rental income to qualify?</summary><p>Often yes, depending on the loan program. Rental income may be reviewed through leases, market rent schedules, or DSCR calculations.</p></details><details><summary>Are investment property rates higher?</summary><p>Investment property pricing is often different from primary residence pricing. The final quote depends on the full scenario.</p></details><details><summary>Can I buy an Airbnb property with financing?</summary><p>Possibly, but short-term rental rules, building restrictions, income assumptions, and lender guidelines need to be reviewed carefully.</p></details></div></div></section><section class="section related-section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Keep comparing</p><h2>Related mortgage pages</h2><div class="card-grid small-grid"><a class="mini-card" href="dscr-loans-miami.html">DSCR Loans Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="cash-out-refinance-miami.html">Cash-Out Refinance Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="condo-loans-miami.html">Condo Loans Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="bank-statement-loans-miami.html">Bank Statement Loans Miami<span>→</span></a></div></div></section></main>
